    {
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "$Source"
      },
      "description": "Client connections rejected for exceeding the per-IP connection limit. The Go relay (nitro-node) exports `arb_feed_clients_limited`; the rust relay (arb-relay, v0.5+) exports `arb_feed_clients_limit_rejected` for `--ip-connections-limit`. Only one series exists per relay job, so a flat line on one of them is expected — but *both* empty means the relay is older than v0.5 or the limiter is inert, not that nothing is being rejected. Check **IP Limit Enforcement** before reading this as zero.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "stacking": {}
          }
        },
        "overrides": null
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_limited{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "limited (go relay) - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_limit_rejected{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "limit rejected (rust relay) - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Connection Limit Rate",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "$Source"
      },
      "description": "Why the rust relay's `--ip-connections-limit` did or did not apply to a connection. **unknown ip** — the `--client-ip-header` was missing, so the limit was *not enforced*; a configured limiter that is inert shows up here. **malformed ip header** — the header could not be parsed, so the limit was enforced against the TCP peer address (typically the proxy, i.e. shared across clients). **exempt ip** — client IP is private or loopback. Sustained unknown/malformed rates mean the rejection count in **Connection Limit Rate** understates reality. Empty on Go relays and on rust relays before v0.5.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "stacking": {}
          }
        },
        "overrides": null
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_limit_unknown_ip{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "unknown ip (limit NOT enforced) - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_malformed_ip_header{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "malformed ip header (fell back to peer) - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_limit_exempt_ip{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "exempt ip (private/loopback) - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "IP Limit Enforcement (rust relay)",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
