    {
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "$Source"
      },
      "description": "Pod egress divided by connected clients — the average bandwidth one feed subscriber costs. Useful for capacity work (egress per additional client) and for spotting a feed whose per-client cost has jumped. Two caveats: the numerator is *total* pod egress from cAdvisor, so it also carries metric scrapes, health checks and upstream chatter — a fixed overhead that is negligible at thousands of clients but dominates at a handful (the arb1 Go feeds sit at ~12 KB/s with zero clients attached). And at zero connected clients the ratio is undefined, so the line breaks rather than spiking.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "stacking": {}
          },
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": null
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(container_network_transmit_bytes_total{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\"}[$__rate_interval]) and on (pod) arb_feed_clients_current{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}) by (cluster) / (sum(arb_feed_clients_current{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}) by (cluster) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "per connection - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Bandwidth per Connection",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "$Source"
      },
      "description": "Client connections admitted per second, split by whether they asked for `permessage-deflate` (`arb_feed_clients_compression_negotiated` / `arb_feed_clients_compression_not_requested`). **negotiated** is uptake, not delivery: a client that negotiates and then fails to inflate still counts. **not requested** is counted whatever the `--compression` setting is, so while it keeps climbing some client is not asking. Under `--compression=off` negotiated is pinned at zero and every connection lands in not requested. Empty on Go relays and on rust relays before v0.7.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "stacking": {}
          }
        },
        "overrides": null
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_compression_negotiated{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "negotiated - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(arb_feed_clients_compression_not_requested{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (cluster)",
          "legendFormat": "not requested - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Compression Negotiation (rust relay)",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "$Source"
      },
      "description": "Share of connections admitted since pod start that negotiated compression. Read the inverse as the pre-flight for `--compression=required`: at 97% uptake, `required` would refuse the remaining 3%. Before flipping it, identify who they are — a chained arb-relay never offers compression on its own upstream connection, so it sits in the refused population. Counters are cumulative, so this resets when a pod restarts. Empty on Go relays and on rust relays before v0.7.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "stacking": {}
          },
          "max": 100,
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": null
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "100 * sum(arb_feed_clients_compression_negotiated{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}) by (cluster) / (sum(arb_feed_clients_compression_negotiated{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"} + arb_feed_clients_compression_not_requested{cluster=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespacepattern\", job=\"$relayjob\"}) by (cluster) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "negotiated - {{cluster}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Compression Uptake % (rust relay)",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
