      "description": "Upstream feed divergence as seen by the rust relay — the fastest way to clear or implicate the relay during a feed incident. **reorgs** are confirmed (changed `blockHash`) replacements; **possible reorgs** are replacements of undetermined severity; **below-confirmed reorgs** changed a blockHash for an already-confirmed, trimmed sequence number and *cannot be rebroadcast* (counts messages, so a replaying upstream re-counts each pass); **flaps** are benign feed flaps. Any non-zero reorg rate here means the divergence originates upstream of the relay. Empty on Go relays.",
